A receiver lost the chunk before the attach command (DR03): the other nodes attach it, the receiver fails the command, sets files seqno 0 and Galera aborts it; the watchdog restarts it and it joins by SST with the rows. Recorded as it behaves today.
––– input –––
export BULK_PAUSE_1=15000; echo ok
––– output –––
ok
––– block: ../base/replication/bulk-cluster-setup –––
––– input –––
source /tmp/bc.sh; load 1 t 1 1000 > /tmp/l1.out & waitpause 1 1; echo "paused $?"; rm -rf $(find /var/log/manticore-3 -maxdepth 3 -name 'repl-*' -type d); echo "node 3 repl=$(repl 3)"
––– output –––
paused 0
node 3 repl=0
––– input –––
wait; cat /tmp/l1.out; source /tmp/bc.sh; waitsynced 3 1; echo "synced $?"; st t
––– output –––
synced 0
node 1: synced count=1000 sum=500500 last_committed=2 files_seqno=2 repl=0
node 2: synced count=1000 sum=500500 last_committed=2 files_seqno=2 repl=0
node 3: synced count=1000 sum=500500 last_committed=2 files_seqno=2 repl=0
––– input –––
L=/var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log; chk() { grep -qE -- "$2" $L && echo "yes: $1" || echo "no: $1"; }; chk 'not prepared' "was not attached on this node, files seqno set to 0: bulk_import chunk [0-9]+ of table 't' is not prepared on this node"; chk 'galera commit failed' 'Commit failed'; chk 'aborted' 'abort from replication provider'; chk 'restarted' 'main process [0-9]+ killed dirtily with signal 6, will be restarted'; chk 'sst at start' "startup SST guard for 'v1': local files seqno 0, remote files seqno 2, force sst 1"
––– output –––
yes: not prepared
yes: galera commit failed
yes: aborted
yes: restarted
yes: sst at start
––– comment –––
Starts of the watchdog and crash dumps of every node; node 3 came back by a watchdog restart after the abort (DR03); the others started once; no crash dump anywhere
––– input –––
for n in 1 2 3; do L=/var/log/manticore-$n/searchd.log; echo "node $n starts=$(grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok' $L) killed=$(grep -c 'killed dirtily' $L) dumps=$(grep -c 'CRASH DUMP' $L)"; done
